# HTTPS vhost - DISABLED BY DEFAULT.
#
# Kept here, commented, instead of in a second file: enabling TLS is then one
# uncomment plus one port publish, and no other file in the stack changes.
# (GPTHub's template is HTTPS-only because it always terminates TLS; this stack
# must also work on a plain :8088 for a first local run.)
#
# To enable:
#   1. Put a certificate at infra/nginx/certs/certificate.pem and its key at
#      infra/nginx/certs/private.pem. compose mounts ../infra/nginx/certs at
#      /etc/nginx/certs (mirror of R:\GPTHub\docker\docker-compose.yaml:156);
#      that directory is gitignored (.gitignore:45) because private keys never
#      enter history.
#   2. Uncomment the server block below and, in the :80 server above, replace
#      `location / { proxy_pass $frontend_upstream; ... }` with a 301 redirect to
#      https://$host$request_uri, keeping the exact-match /health location
#      unredirected so probes keep working.
#   3. Publish the port: set NGINX_PUBLISH_HTTPS in docker/.env.<mode> and add
#      the publish entry to the gateway service (${NGINX_PUBLISH_HTTPS:-8443}:443,
#      the same shape as R:\GPTHub\docker\docker-compose.yaml:165).
